.TH "PB-UPDATE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-update - Update pb from the signed Paperboat release


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb update [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Update pb from the signed Paperboat release

.PP
Download and verify a signed Paperboat release, then review and approve its exact candidate before installation. Check and status are read-only; download never restarts services. Updates preserve existing terminal sessions and established managed SSH connections, wait for finite operations to finish, and restart previews and tunnels. The first migration from an older runtime requires its work to stop. --force permits interrupting work that cannot be preserved; artifact verification and rollback protection still apply. --from installs a local or HTTPS executable, package, or authenticated offline bundle. Bare supplied builds are custom; bundles retain official provenance.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--approve\fP=""
	install the exact downloaded candidate ID after reviewing it

.PP
\fB--force\fP[=false]
	install now, allowing interruption of work that cannot be preserved

.PP
\fB--from\fP=""
	install an executable, package, or verified offline bundle from a local path or HTTPS URL

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for update

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP, \fBpb-update-bundle(1)\fP, \fBpb-update-check(1)\fP, \fBpb-update-download(1)\fP, \fBpb-update-settings(1)\fP, \fBpb-update-status(1)\fP
